==Finnish==
{{Finnish index|l|o}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|fi|urj-fpr-pro|*lowna}} ("day, midday"). Cognates include {{cog|krl|lounat||evening/main meal}}, {{cog|vep|louna}}, {{cog|vot|lõunaz||south, lunch}}, {{cog|et|lõuna||south, lunch}} and {{cog|koi|лун}}. Permic cognates have the meaning "day", whereas Baltic-Finnic cognates denote the direction where the Sun is at midday or the meal eaten at midday.

The compass point meaning was clarified in the 19th century; in earlier text and dialects ''lounas'' may mean either south, southwest or southeast. Compare {{l|fi|lounatuuli||southern wind}}. <ref>{{R:Hakkinen 2004}}</ref>

